-- haxe-parity Task 1 (modules): a cross-module call through `use`.
-- `greet` (this fixture's own `greet/` subdirectory) is a project-
-- relative module, resolved by directory — not one of the six reserved
-- stdlib namespaces. `greet.hello()` lowers exactly like a bare free-fn
-- call (emit.ml): the `use` alias's only job was proving, at typecheck
-- time, that the reference was legitimately in scope.
use greet

fn main() {
  print(greet.hello())
}
